<!--
objective.md.template — minimal objective-file contract run_loop.sh consumes generically.
Copy this file (e.g. to <project>/objectives/my-slice.md), fill in the fields, then run:

    run_loop.sh --objective objectives/my-slice.md

Format: plain `key: value` lines (one value per line, no YAML/JSON parser — shell-only).
`#`-prefixed lines and blank lines are ignored. CLI flags on run_loop.sh
(--level/--lane/--from/--until-commit/--max-rounds/--timeout/--repo) override the matching
field below when both are given. Only `check_cmd` is required.
-->

# Objective: <short title>

goal: <one-line statement of what "done" means>

acceptance: <prose — the exact gate(s)/criteria a human would check to call this done>

check_cmd: <command that proves the objective is met; run inside the repo each round, e.g. "npm run typecheck && npm test">

artifacts: none

lane: <tmux session name run_loop.sh dispatches the round prompt into; leave empty for a checks-only run against the current repo state, no dispatch>

from: <SHA the run starts from>

until_commit: <SHA that marks completion once check_cmd passes there; leave empty to complete the first round check_cmd passes>

level: L2

max_rounds: 10

timeout_mins: 10

prompt: <single-line prompt/command sent into the lane each round via `tmux send-keys`>
